  "policies": {
    "Godfrey": "The actual accepted original minion Battlecry deals base 2 MINION_ABILITY damage to all other current living active minions in one shared health batch. After ordinary reactions, deaths, Deathrattles and Reborn, repeat on the new board only if a genuine board-minion death has a damage/poison cause from this exact wave.",
    "Source": "Exclude the physical Battlecry carrier on every wave. Accepted Battlecry continues after source death, silence, control change or movement; original physical source allocation is frozen per damage batch. No fake SPELL CAST and no spell-damage bonus.",
    "Receipt": "Each continuation binds its original active Battlecry, source allocation, complete ordered original physical victim group, health batch identity and complete damage-result ID range. Queued restoration rejects substituted, clipped or future receipts. All health, death, RNG, selection and terminal limits stay in the existing interpreter."
  },
  "uncertainties": [
    "Each wave waits for ordinary health reactions, deaths, Deathrattles and Reborn before capturing the next current board. The precise official damage/death notification order remains deferred CN calibration.",
    "Only actual minion damage/poison deaths attributable to this original batch cause a repeat; unrelated destruction and later reaction damage deaths are excluded. This exact boundary is explicit local policy pending CN calibration.",
    "Original accepted Battlecry survives loss, silence, transformation or control changes of its carrier. Each later damage packet still uses the shared executor and its then-current physical source facts.",
    "No arbitrary successful wave cap: ordinary resolution budgets and terminal stopping remain authoritative, and budget exhaustion rolls back rather than reporting a shortened success.",
    "Teron remains the next required original destroyed-group memory dependency. Full past 732 candidates and all other special-pool domains remain open; this card is not a complete past pool or an official standard eligibility claim."
  ]
